> "You can't pay vendor bills with open receivables. But AR financing done right will pay for steady growth."
>
> Serve Funding

## Michael's Memo: The Right AR Financing for Healthy Yet Rapid Growth

We've all met business owners with a warehouse full of inventory or a ledger full of unpaid invoices: assets that look strong on paper but can't cover payroll or fund a new contract tomorrow.

Here's the thing. Financing against accounts receivable isn't just a last resort for supposedly struggling companies. It's a strategic tool that healthy, growing businesses use to fuel healthy, steady growth.

Give us a call if you:

- Have strong sales but slow-paying customers, 30 to 90 days
- Need payroll covered before a contract payment arrives
- Win a big order but can't fund materials until invoices clear
- Are in staffing, construction, manufacturing, or government contracting
- Have maxed your bank line but are still growing. We have second-lien AR financing options.

By financing your AR, whether factoring or an asset-backed revolver, you're opting for a smart, proactive way to access the capital you've already earned.

Let's keep growing,

Michael Kodinsky, Founder & CEO

## Deal Highlight: $1MM AR Line With Unbeatable Structure and Pricing

A healthcare supply manufacturer in Central Florida was growing slowly but steadily. Several banks passed on growth financing because of a net loss on the last tax return. One of those bankers introduced them to Serve Funding just as the company entered rapid expansion with its largest customer, whose invoices made up 80 to 90% of monthly orders.

In under three weeks we helped them close a $1,000,000 facility leveraging just that one customer's receivables, expanded to $1.5MM within two months: 92% advance rate, a 0.25% purchase fee on new invoices, and Prime + 2% on funds drawn. Better than a term loan, this revolving structure grows with the firm month after month.

The full story is in the case study: [$1MM Invoice Factoring at Single-Digit Rates](/blog/ar-financing-healthcare-supply).

## Creative Capital Solution: Fast, Flexible Funding From Your Invoices

**What it is:** accounts receivable financing converts unpaid invoices into immediate working capital. Instead of waiting 30, 60, or 90 days for customer payments, you can access most of that cash in days.

**Product snapshot:**

- Funding: up to 90% of invoice value advanced immediately
- Speed to close: often within 10 to 15 business days, faster in some cases
- Structure: factoring (sell the invoice) or financing (borrow against it)
- Terms: flexible, spot funding or an ongoing facility
- Industries: construction, manufacturing, staffing, healthcare, CPG, B2B services, government contracting, and more

**Why it works:** it smooths cash flow for payroll, inventory, or new projects, keeps growth on track without adding long-term debt, lets you fund only the invoices that make sense, and in the right structure costs can be comparable to an SBA loan.

**Best fit:** high-growth businesses with long customer payment cycles, seasonal or project-based businesses needing upfront capital, and companies waiting on large contract payments.

## More Than Money: Core Value of the Month, Thankfulness

At Serve Funding, thankfulness is more than a polite thank you. It's the mindset we bring to every relationship.

We are deeply grateful for the business leaders who invite us into their growth journey, for the bankers and advisors who trust us with the people they serve, and for the vetted lenders in our network delivering creative and timely solutions.

Thankfulness keeps us grounded, collaborative, and focused on the bigger picture, not just the transaction. It reminds us that every funded deal represents someone's dream moving forward. When we lead with gratitude, we strengthen relationships, create better outcomes, and keep the human in every handshake.
